      "id": "OI-01",
      "question": "Section 3 makes Groq or Cerebras the llm.fast primary, but neither appears in the W3 onboarding provider list (DeepInfra, Fireworks, Z.ai, DeepSeek, aggregator). Which host serves llm.fast's primary leg, and is it added to W3?",
      "blocks": "llm.fast primary reachability; W5-03 canary for llm.fast",
      "owner": "CEO"
    },
    {
      "id": "OI-02",
      "question": "Section 3 names a Fable-class primary for llm.agentic, but the lumic model registry's strongest registered Anthropic model is claude-opus-4-7. Register a Fable-class model in @adaptic/lumic-utils, or accept opus-4-7 as the llm.agentic primary?",
      "blocks": "llm.agentic primary fidelity to Section 3",
      "owner": "CEO"
    },
    {
      "id": "OI-03",
      "question": "Every alias budget is provisional-pre-baseline because Section 9's baseline monthly spend is still FILL. Which caps apply once W1-03 produces the billing baseline?",
      "blocks": "PD-7 layer 3 calibration; Section 9 savings target measurement",
      "owner": "CEO"
    },
    {
      "id": "OI-04",
      "question": "llm.agentic's serving chain is one leg long because Section 3 makes its primary the closed incumbent and its only secondary shadow-eval-only. An Anthropic outage therefore leaves the alias with no configured fallback. Widen it (a second closed provider, or promoting the Kimi leg out of shadow), or accept the single leg?",
      "blocks": "llm.agentic availability under a primary-provider outage",
      "owner": "CEO"
    }
  ]
